# The network of "Three sites": the shop's triangle of routers, and r1's
# link to the internet through an ISP.
#
#   office 10.1.0.10 --- r1 ---------- r2 --- store 10.2.0.10
#                        | \          /
#                        |  \        /
#                        |      r3 --- dc 10.3.0.10 (a web server)
#                        |
#             wan 198.51.100.2
#                        |
#             isp 198.51.100.1 --- web 203.0.113.10 (a web server)
#
# Each router's interfaces are named after what is at the far end of the
# cable. The hosts have a default route to their own router; the routers
# start with no routes beyond their own networks, and their routes belong
# in FRR. There is no NAT in this topic, so the ISP carries the shop's
# private addresses back to r1, as a provider's private network service
# would; on the internet, the next topic's NAT would be needed instead.
machine office
machine store
machine dc
machine r1 router
machine r2 router
machine r3 router
machine isp router
machine web

link office:eth0=10.1.0.10/24 r1:lan=10.1.0.1/24
link store:eth0=10.2.0.10/24 r2:lan=10.2.0.1/24
link dc:eth0=10.3.0.10/24 r3:lan=10.3.0.1/24
link r1:r2=10.0.12.1/30 r2:r1=10.0.12.2/30
link r1:r3=10.0.13.1/30 r3:r1=10.0.13.2/30
link r2:r3=10.0.23.1/30 r3:r2=10.0.23.2/30
link r1:wan=198.51.100.2/24 isp:shop=198.51.100.1/24
link isp:web=203.0.113.1/24 web:eth0=203.0.113.10/24

route office default via 10.1.0.1
route store default via 10.2.0.1
route dc default via 10.3.0.1
route web default via 203.0.113.1
route isp 10.0.0.0/8 via 198.51.100.2

run r1 frr
run r2 frr
run r3 frr
run dc nginx
run web nginx
